1 NOTE {geni:about_me} When Uzun Hassan died in 1478 he was succeeded by his son Khalil Mirza (r. 1478-79).Khalil was defeated one year later by a confederation under his younger brother Yaqub.
2 CONT
2 CONT (r.1479-91). Then a war of succession broke out among Uzun Hassan’s grandsons about thesupremacy, and the empire was again divided among the princes into several spheres of interests.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sultan Klialll (governor of Fars during his father's life time) succeeded to the throne,  and appointed his brother, Ya'qiib Mirza, governor of Diyar Bakr. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sultan Khalil proved weak, and the nobles of his court declared for Ya'qiib Mirza,  who, thereupon, advanced on Adharbayjan. In the ensuing battle near Marand,  on Rabi' II, 14, 883 "/July 15, 1478, Sultan Khalil lost his life and
2 CONC  Ya'qiib Mirza,  occupied Tabriz.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ya'qiib Mirzii ascended the throne. Ahmad Beg ibn Sultan Khalil and Kusa  Hajji Bayandar, rose in revolt at Shiror. and Isfahan respectively, but the rebellions  were easily suppressed. Similarly, in 886/1481-82, Bayandar Beg rose
2 CONC  in revolt at  Isfahan, but was killed by the king's vanguard commanded by Sufi Khalil. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ref. https://archive.org/stream/HistoryOfShahIsmailSafawi-GhulamSarwar/119900259-History-of-Shah-Isma-il-Safawi-Ghulam-Sarwar_djvu.txt
