2 CONC he fort of Alanjiq 8 ; but  another potential rival Mahamud Beg 6 ibn Ughurlfi Muhammad fled to Shah 'All  Parnak at Hamadan, where the Khutba was read in his name. Finally, Mahmud Beg  advanced on Adharbayjan, and encountered Bay
2 CONC sunqur Mirzii at Darguzm, but was  defeated in battle, and put to death after capture. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After this victory, Sufi Khalil, commander-in-chiei of Baysunqur Mirza, assumed  great power, which invoked the resentment of other nobles " . In the end of 896 8 /  about Oct., 1491, Sulayman Beg, governor of Diyar Bakr, advanced
