1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catherine_Cornaro   ''(43 langues)''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Catherine Cornaro''' (Greek: Αικατερίνη Κορνάρο; Venetian: Catarina Corner) (25 November 1454 – 10 July 1510) was the last monarch of the Kingdom of Cyprus, also holding the titles of Queen of Jerusalem and Queen of Armenia. Sh
2 CONC e became queen consort of Cyprus by marriage to James II of Cyprus, and then regent of Cyprus during the minority of her son James III of Cyprus in 1473–1474, and finally queen regnant of Cyprus upon his death. She reigned from 26
2 CONC  August 1474 to 26 February 1489 and was declared a "Daughter of Saint Mark" in order that the Republic of Venice could claim control of Cyprus after the death of her husband. .. ... 
2 CONT
2 CONT The last Crusader state became a colony of Venice, and as compensation, Catherine was allowed to retain the title of queen and was made lady of Asolo, a county on the Terraferma[13] of the Republic of Venice in the Veneto region, 
2 CONC in 1489. Asolo soon gained a reputation as a court of literary and artistic distinction, mainly as a result of it being the fictitious setting for Pietro Bembo's platonic dialogues on love, Gli Asolani. Catherine lived in Asolo un
2 CONC til 1509, when the League of Cambrai sacked the town, then fled to Venice where she lived for another year, dying on 10 July 1510.[14] She is entombed in the Church of San Salvador in Venice. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Still to be found the connection between https://www.geni.com/people/Catherine-Cornaro-queen-of-Cyprus/6000000008467548795 and her "cousin":   https://www.geni.com/people/Giorgio-I-Contarini-count-of-Jaffa-Ascalon/6000000080117603
2 CONC 855 (This [https://www.geni.com/path/Catherine-Cornaro-queen-of-Cyprus+is+related+to+Giorgio-I-Contarini-count-of-Jaffa-Ascalon?from=6000000008467548795&path_type=inlaw&to=6000000080117603855 relationship path]?)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''San Salvador Interno - Tomb of Caterina Cornaro'''
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2d/San_Salvador_Interno_-_Tomb_of_Caterina_Cornaro.jpg|center|alt=San Salvador Interno - Tomb of Caterina Cornaro}}
2 CONT
2 CONT >Source: ''Church of San Salvador, in Venice - The tombstone of Catherine Cornaro.'' < [https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:San_Salvador_Interno_-_Tomb_of_Caterina_Cornaro.jpg Wikimedia Commons] > CCA-SA 4.0 license
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT # https://www.britannica.com/topic/Contarini-family '''Contarini family,''' distinguished Venetian family, one of the 12 that elected the first doge in 697 and later gave Venice eight doges and many other eminent citizens. There w
2 CONC ere at one time no fewer than 18 branches of the family; one of the most important was that of Contarini dallo Zaffo, or di Giaffa, who had been invested with the countship of Jaffa in Syria for their services to Caterina Cornaro,
2 CONC  queen of Cyprus; ...
2 CONT # http://cardinaliserenissima.uniud.it/images/genogrammi/corner_new.jpg 
