1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * From [https://books.google.com/books?id=JNNQCgAAQBAJ&pg=PA61&lpg=PA61&dq=helene+of+kakheti&source=bl&ots=y8JIzV-2NE&sig=wd3HIVhzw1as0lWpj6xSq-0WsY8&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwjRkMXo1-zPAhWJeSYKHbMBCo0Q6AEIOzAF#v=onepa
2 CONC ge&q=helene%20of%20kakheti&f=false '''Historical Dictionary of Georgia'''], by Alexander Mikaberidze:
2 CONT
2 CONT Shah Abbas also surrounded himself with many Georgian nobles, appointing them to key positions throughout Persia. Among his wives were Leila, the sister of King Luarsab II of Kartli; Helene, sister of King Teimuraz I of Kakheti; a
2 CONC nd Fahrimjan Begum, sister of King Simon I of Kartli.
2 CONT ====
2 CONT
2 CONT [...Paykar Khān Igīrmī Dūrt  rose to influence in 1608, when Shah Abbas I appointed him governor of Barda. Around 1620, he was, further, given the governorship of Kakheti, a neighboring Georgian kingdom, which the shah sought to b
2 CONC ring under his full control. On this occasion, Abbas gave to Paykar in marriage Lela (Fatma Sultan Begum),[2] a royal princess from another Georgian kingdom, that of Kartli, whom the shah dismissed from his harem after having her 
2 CONC brother, King Luarsab II of Kartli, executed. ] ref https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paykar_Khan_Igirmi_Durt
