1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In 1704, he was appointed beglerbeg of the Kandahar province by the Safavid Shah, while he was already governor of Kerman. . Gorgin Khan, once establishedl in Kandahar, met his match in the person of Mir Wais, the 
2 CONC head of the Hotaki tribe of the Afghan tribe the Gilzis who also mayor of the city]...[Mir Wais must have been livid when in 1706 he was relieved of his supervisory post. Gorgin Khan's behavior in Kandahar only exacerbated the sit
2 CONC uation, as his harsh rule antagonized the Sunni Afghans... His soldiers misbehaved towards the local population: he sequestered goods, commandeered Afghan girls and women and raised taxes. Gorgin Khan is said to have partied on 8 
2 CONC June I709, the day of the murder of the caliph Omar Mo'men Kermani. There are also stories of how the Shi,ite Georgians would bring pigs into mosques and drink inside, how they would abuse underage girls aged nine to ten years old
2 CONC  to to the point of killing them, and then would dump the bodies at their parents' homes. The resentful Afghans sent several complaints to Isfahan, but these were intercepted by Gorgin Khan's men at court and thus never reached th
2 CONC e shah. In the end, the Afghans acted on their own by rebelling against their Georgian over lords. This gave Gorgin Khan an excuse to arrest Mir Wais and to send him to Isfahan, urging the shah to get rid of him or at least never 
2 CONC to allow him to return to Kandahar. While in Isfahan, Mir Wais, through skillful flattery and substantial bribes, managed to rehabilitate himself and to persuade the shah that Gorgin Khan was untrustworthy and intended to turn Kan
2 CONC dahar into an autonomous region ruled by himself, and that Persia was threatened by an impending coalition between the Russians and the Georgians. Sent back to Kandahar to serve as a shadow administrator, Mir Wais rallied his peop
2 CONC le against the Georgians. Matters came to a head when Gorgin Khan demanded Mir Wais's own daughter.  Gorgin Khan met his death at the hands of the Afghans in 1709, either killed in his tent, after which the Afghans took Kandahar a
2 CONC nd massacred the city's Georgian garrison, or hacked down after the Afghans invited him and his entourage to a banquet. Upon Gorgin Khan's death, Kay Khosrow (Khosrow Khan) https://www.geni.com/people/Kay-Khosrow Bagrationi/600000
2 CONC 0021614418167?through=6000000017602449365 was appointed Sepahsalar and Wali of Georgia and he was sent to Kandahar to avenge his uncle's death.] ref : Academia.edu - Rudolph Matthee, Kandahar.
2 CONT =====
2 CONT [by the early 18th century the state was in serious decline and the reigning shah, Sultan Husayn, was a weak ruler. When Sultan Husayn attempted to quell a rebellion by the Ghilzai Afghans in Kandahar, the governor he sent (Gurgin
2 CONC  Khan) was killed. ]http://www.wikiwand.com/en/Nader_Shah
2 CONT
2 CONT Contemporary of Shah Tahmasp II Safavi - Vakhtang VI (alias Hossein Gholi Khan) and David Bek (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Davit_Bek )
2 CONT http://www.wikiwand.com/en/George_XI_of_Kartli
2 CONT
2 CONT A document says that he died in 1729 [ page 135 of file:///home/chronos/u-3aee9e93dd168931eff71ff99c2a73e8c9317d8b/Downloads/1019-_Turkoloji_Tarix_Qarabaghname_Perviz_Zere_Shahmeresi_Fars_Ebced_Urmu_Turuz_2014.pdf]
2 CONT
2 CONT GURGIN KHAN - Shahnavaz Khan - Constantin - see page 129 of file:///home/chronos/u-3aee9e93dd168931eff71ff99c2a73e8c9317d8b/Downloads/1019-_Turkoloji_Tarix_Qarabaghname_Perviz_Zere_Shahmeresi_Fars_Ebced_Urmu_Turuz_2014.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT Safavid governor of Qandahar until 1709 when he was overthrown by Mīrwais Khān Hotak - a Ghilzai Afghan notable -, Gurgin Khan was a Georgian convert to Islam, originally Giorgi XI and known in his converted state as Gurgin or Sha
2 CONC hnavaz Khan. He was a valued gholam in the Safavid service because of his military skills and sent to Qandahar in 1704 to secure Iran's bastion against Mughul India and prevent local unrest amongst the Afghans. [ref. pages 33 to 3
2 CONC 5 of The Cambridge History of Iran, volume 7].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Gurgin Khan will be murdered after Mīrwais Khān Hotak had a fatwa set against him in Mecca. Mir Vais succeeds him as Governor of Qandahar,. Mirwais Khan is anti Safavid.https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mirwais_Hotak
