2 CONT Ugurlu khan Ziyadoglu-Gajar was appointed beylerbeyi of Karabakh after the death of his brother Murtuzagulu khan in 1664. Ugurlu khan died in 1666.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ugurlu khan had sons named Abbasgulu khan, Kalbali khan, Rzagulu khan.
2 CONT
2 CONT The successful khan was a poet. He wrote poetry under the pseudonym Ziyadi. He patronized poets and provided for them. Literary critic Firudin bey Kocharli writes: "It is clear from an autobiography written in his divan that Govsi
2 CONC  Ugurlu khan lived happily under the protection of Ziyad oglu in his age. However, he did not forget his homeland and always remembered him. It is said that he was his brother and uncle of the famous Javad khan, who ruled in 1180-
2 CONC 1190 AH. "
2 CONT
2 CONT Ziyadi Ganjavi was friends with Govsi Tabrizi. Govsi wrote in his autobiography dedicated to him:
2 CONT
2 CONT Ugurlu khan Ziyad oglu in the life of Musahib that we are his servant, be his servant Solomon.
2 CONT
