2 CONT ... [In the same year, Jandar Kara-Keshish oglu converted to Islam and took the name Alijan. At that time, the askers of the amirs of the Iranian vilayets, taking advantage of the fact that there were no rulers and khans in Sheki,
2 CONC  made night raids on Sheki, robbed and took away many prisoners.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alijan was a very smart, capable and brave man. The Nukha and Sheki inhabitants, having concluded an alliance, elected Alijan as ruler and made him a khan, so that he ruled the Sheki vilayet and protected it from the atrocities of
2 CONC  the Persian robbers; and he ran perfectly. [He] died in 861 (1456-1457).
2 CONT
2 CONT After him, his son became Khan, named Kutul, who, having achieved [by various] means of the Shah’s decree on the Khanate, began to govern the Sheki Vilayet. [He] died in ... 1 g. His son, by the name of Sheki Khan 2 , became Khan 
2 CONC . He died in ...
2 CONT
2 CONT His son Hasan Sultan came into possession of the Sheki Khanate.
2 CONT
