2 CONT The Indian campaign was the zenith of Nader's career. Afterwards he became increasingly despotic as his health declined markedly. Nader had left his son Reza Qoli Mirza to rule Persia in his absence. Reza had behaved highhandedly 
2 CONC and somewhat cruelly but he had kept the peace in Persia. Having heard rumours that his father had died, he had made preparations for assuming the crown. These included the murder of the former shah Tahmasp and his family, includi
2 CONC ng the nine-year-old Abbas III. On hearing the news, Reza's wife, who was Tahmasp's sister, committed suicide. ref.http://www.wikiwand.com/en/Nader_Shah ref: (The Sword of Persia, Nader Shah from tribal warrior to conquering tyran
2 CONC t - Michael Axworthy) ---------------------
