1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Maulana Kaazim Ali Khan''' (fl. early 19th century) was a Mughal-era official and the father of Maulana Raza Ali Khan. He served as a tax-collector (revenue officer) in the city of Badayun, in present-day Uttar 
2 CONC Pradesh, India. His role placed him within the declining Mughal administrative structure, which still operated at the local level during the early stages of British influence. He was also a Hafiz, which memorised the entire holy Q
2 CONC uran.
