1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grigol_Orbeliani
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Grigol Orbeliani or Jambakur-Orbeliani (Georgian: გრიგოლ ორბელიანი; ჯამბაკურ-ორბელიანი) (October 2, 1804 – March 21, 1883) was a Georgian Romanticist poet and soldier in the Imperial Russian service. One of the most colorfu
2 CONC l figures in the 19th-century Georgian culture, Orbeliani is noted for his patriotic poetry, lamenting Georgia's lost past and independent monarchy. At the same time, he spent decades in the Russian military service, rising throug
2 CONC h ranks to highest positions in the imperial administration in the Caucasus.
