2 CONT iii) Prince Aleksandri Bagrationi [Kniaz '''Alexander Ivanovitch Bagration''']. Granted the hereditary title of Kniaz Bagration by Emperor Paul of Russia, 4th October 1800 o.s. He had issue, three sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) Lieutenant-General H.E. Prince Petri Bagrationi [Kniaz Peotr Alexandrovitch Bagration]. b. 24th September 1818. ADC to General Vitivtov at Erivan 1805, prom. Lieut-Gen. 1835, ADC to the Emperor and Governor-General of the Balt
2 CONC ic States. m. Princess Anna Alexeievna (b. 13th August 1823 o.s.; d. 27th June 1908 o.s.), daughter of Alexei Mikhailovitch Martinov, by his wife, Elisaveta Vassilievna, daughter of Vassili Muratov. He d. 17th January 1876, having
2 CONC  had issue, two sons and three daughters: Copyright ©Christopher Buyers
2 CONT (a) Major-General H.E. Prince Demetre Bagrationi [Kniaz Dimitri Petrovitch Bagration]. b. 13th June 1863 o.s. Cmsnd. 2nd-Lieut. Vladimir Lncrs., Chief Adj. Sch. of Equitation for Ofcrs. m. Princess Vera Mikhailovna, daughter of Mi
2 CONC khail Zakharin. He d. in a Bolshevik prison, 1918/1919, having had issue, an only daughter:
2 CONT (i) Princess Nino Bagrationi [Kniaza Nina Dimitrievna Bagration].
2 CONT (b) Colonel Prince Aleksandri Bagrationi [Kniaz Alexander Petrovitch Bagration]. He d. in a Bolshevik prison, 1918/1919.
2 CONT (a) Princess Evgenia Bagrationi [Kniaza Evgenia Petrovna Bagration]. b. 30th October 1846 o.s. She d. at St Petersburg, 19th September 1903 o.s.
2 CONT (b) Princess Elizabed [Kniaza Elisaveta Petrovna]. b. 1847. m. before 1864, Eric-Georges de Goldbeck (d. 1876). She d. ca. 1868.
2 CONT (c) Princess Vera [Kniaza Vera Petrovna] Bagration.
2 CONT
2 CONT (2) Prince Nikolaoz Bagrationi [Kniaz Nikolai Alexandrovitch Bagration].
2 CONT
2 CONT (3) Colonel Prince Ramaz Bagrationi [Kniaz Roman Alexandrovitch Bagration]. Cmsnd. 2nd-Lieut. Sappers of the Imperial Guards.
