2 CONT ii) Lieutenant-General H.E. Prince Ramaz Bagrationi [Kniaz Roman Ivanovitch Bagration]. b. 1784. Cdr. of a Cav. dvsn. Granted the hereditary title of Kniaz Bagration by Emperor Paul of Russia, 4th October 1800 o.s. m. Princess Ann
2 CONC a Simenovna, daughter of Simen Ivanov. He d. at Tiflis, 2nd March 1834 (bur. St David's Church), having had issue, two sons and one daughter: 
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) Prince Petri Bagrationi [Kniaz Peotr Ramazovitch Bagration]. Chemist. He had issue, an only daughter:
2 CONT (a) Princess Elizabed Bagrationi [Kniaza Elisaveta Petrovna  Bagration]. b. 23rd August 1864. She d. unm. 2nd March 1894.
2 CONT
2 CONT (2) Colonel Prince Ioani Bagrationi [Kniaz Ivan Ramazovitch Bagration]. He was k-i-a. in the Caucasus, before 1890, having had issue, one son:
2 CONT (a) Prince Ramaz Bagrationi [Kniaz Roman Ivanovitch Bagration]. Lieut. Russian service 1835.
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) Princess Elizabed [Kniaza Elisaveta Romanovna]. m. Lieutenant-General H.E. Baron Alexander Nikolaievitch Belendorff [or Böhlendorf] (d. at St Petersburg, 17th November 1882 o.s.). She d. at St Petersburg, 27th July 1867.
