1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Grand son of an Armenian priest who converted to Islam. He had four sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hasan agha - died in battle against Amir Aslan khan of Afsharid army [( aka Najafqulu Khan I (Born 1696 — died 1748) was the first khan of the Tabriz Khanate from 1747 to 1784.[)] Aghakishi beg - viceroy of Ganja and next khan of 
2 CONC Shaki. Abdulgadir khan Jafar agha
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_of_Black_Monk
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shaki_Khanate
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a distant offspring of Hasan Sultan of the House of Black Monk https://www.geni.com/people/Hasan-Soltan-of-the-House-of-Black-Monk-Khan-of-Sheki-d-1524/6000000044122042287.  Nader Shah who wanted to subdue the people of Sha
2 CONC ki, attacked it in 1744 and sieged the Gelersen-Gorersen fortress where Haji Chalabi took refuge. The name of the fortress Gələrsən Görərsən which means in Azerbaijani language "Come and see" derives from the historic episode rela
2 CONC ted to the siege. When Nader Shah sent an ultimatum to surrender, Haji Chelebi sent a response letter saying "Come and see". Outraged shah ordered to destroy the rest of the town. After the death of Nader Shah, Haji Chelebi took r
2 CONC evenge by going south as far as Tabriz. Haji Chalabi Khan died from illness in 1755. According to other sources, he died as a result of assassination plot organized by other khans of the area. He had three sons: Aghakishi Khan, Ha
2 CONC ji Abdulgadir and Jafar Agha. Aghakishi Khan succeeded his father as the ruler of Shaki Khanate.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haji_Chalabi_Khan
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://www.vostlit.info/Texts/rus16/Chadzi_Seid_Abdulhamid/text.phtml?id=2210
2 CONT
2 CONT Chelebi Khan, son of Kendhuda Kurban, son of Alidjan, son of Asker bey, son of Alijan bey, son of Bagi bey, son of Dervish Muhammad Khan ... Haji Chelebi Khan fell ill and died in 1168 [(1754-1755)]. After him three sons remained:
2 CONC  Aga Kishi Khan, Haji Abdulkadir and Jafar Agha, and one grandson, Hussein Khan, the son of a man killed in the war [with Iran ] Hasan agi, [60] After Haji Chelebi khan, his son Aga Kishi khan became the ruler in Nukh; [he] was ma
2 CONC rried to the daughter of Muhammad Khan of Kumuk.
2 CONT ====
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haji_Chalabi_Khan
2 CONT
2 CONT Born to a certain landlord Gurban beg during the reign of Sultan Husayn in 1703, he was of noble birth. Brockhaus and Efron Encyclopedic Dictionary cites a legend calling him the grandson of an Armenian priest who converted to Isl
2 CONC am.[1] Biographer Haji Seyid Abdulhamid mentions him as a 7th generation descendant of Darvish Mohammad Khan,[2] last khan of Shaki before Safavid Invasion of Shirvan. Petrushevsky also thought of him being either Udi or Armenian 
2 CONC origin.[3] There are also some indications that he may have been descended from Shirvanshahs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebellion against Nader Shah
2 CONT He was supported by locals in opposition to corrupt Afsharid appointed viceroy Malik Najaf. His name was frequently mentioned in annals regarding to Nader's Dagestan campaign. He was confirmed by Nader as an overseer to check corr
2 CONC uption of Malik Najaf. However viceroy protested against it, causing locals to rebel. In course of rebellion, despite losing 500 families to Nader, Chalabi managed to murder Malik Najaf in 1743.[4] To punish disobedience, Nader at
2 CONC tacked Shaki in 1744 and sieged the Galarsan-Gorarsan fortress where Haji Chalabi took refuge. The name of the fortress Gələrsən Görərsən which means in Azerbaijani language "Come and see" derives from the historic episode related
2 CONC  to the siege. When Nader Shah sent an ultimatum to surrender, Chalabi sent a response letter saying "Come and see". Outraged shah ordered to destroy the rest of the town. He successfully defended against a second attack from Nade
2 CONC r in February 1745. However he submitted to Nader in March 1746, asking for forgiveness. Nader approved his submission and forgave him, appointing Malik Najaf's nephew Malik Jafar as new governor and Haji Chalabi as his overseer.
2 CONT
2 CONT He declared his independence as the khan when Nader was murdered in 1747. Using power vacuum, Chalabi raided south as far as Tabriz and became a major power in the region with strong army. His first target was Karabakh in 1748, wh
2 CONC ere he made an alliance of Melikdoms of Karabakh and rival branches of Javanshir clan, although nothing came out of it. Alarmed local rulers, namely Panah khan of Karabakh, Heydargulu khan of Nakhchivan, Shahverdi khan of Ganja, K
2 CONC azim khan of Karadagh concluded alliance against Shaki Khanate. They were invited by Teimuraz II who wished to join their alliance, but in fact capturing them as hostages, demanding tributes. Having received the news, Chalabi khan
2 CONC  and his army rushed to the aid of their former enemies. His forces prevailed in the battle against Georgian prince Heraclius in June 1752 near Aghstafa river and routed them to Tbilisi. Chalabi khan appointed his son Aghakishi be
2 CONC g as viceroy to newly conquered territories of Ganja, Kazakh and Borchali. Subsequently, in 1755, in an attempt to establish his hegemony over the Shirvan Khanate, Haji Chalabi was defeated by Huseynali khan of Quba and the result
2 CONC  of this defeat was the decline of the power of Sheki Khanate. Chalabi died same year from an illness.
2 CONT He was a zealous ruler and known to be imposed a double tax on Udi population called "din ipəyi".[5]Gilahli Mosque was built on the order of Haji Chalabi in 1749.
