2 CONT Prince Nikoloz "Tato" Baratashvili (Georgian: ნიკოლოზ "ტატო" ბარათაშვილი) (December 4, 1817 - October 21, 1845) was a Georgian poet, one of the first Georgians to marry a modern nationalism with European Romanticism and to introdu
2 CONC ce "Europeanism" into Georgian literature. Despite his early death and a tiny literary heritage of fewer than forty short lyrics, one extended poem, and a few private letters, Baratashvili is considered to be the high point of Geo
2 CONC rgian Romanticism. He was referred as the "Georgian Byron".
