1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marina Sagredo was a woman famous for the freedom and independence of thoughts and attitudes. To her Carlo Goldoni in 1700 dedicated the comedy "La Sposa Virtuosa" and for her Pietro Longhi in 1774 painted L'elefan
2 CONC te, recording the exhibition of the exotic pachyderm during the carnival, according to the documentary praxis inaugurated twenty years earlier with images of Rhinoceros. Pietro Longhihe portrayed in the "Lesson of geography", pain
2 CONC ting of the Civic Museums of Padua, also the daughters of Caterina Sagredo and Gregorio Barbarigo (1709-1766) Cecilia and Contarina Barbarigo the fiery lover of Andrea Memmo .
