2 CONC %D1%80%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D0%A4%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B4%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B4%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B8%D1%87
2 CONT
2 CONT konekäännös:
2 CONT Gregor zu Sayn Wittgenstein-Berleburg
2 CONT syntynyt 19.7.1873  kuollut 25.2.1907 (33v) Pietari, Venäjä, Venäjä /kuolema kurkku ja keuhkot
2 CONT Hautapaikka: Druzhnoselye Village Tsarskoje Seloa lääni, Pietarin lääni, Venäjä, Venäjä
2 CONT
2 CONT Vanhemmat: Ferdinand Wilhelm Emil von Sayn-Wittgestein-Berleburg ja Paraskewa  Alexandrova von Sayn- Wittgenstein-Berleburg (Paronitar)
2 CONT
2 CONT Puoliso: Elisaveta von Sayn-Wittgenstein-Berleburg
2 CONT Lapset;: Nina Zu Say-Wittgenstei-Berleburg
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sayn-Wittgenstein
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT "The very week of the coronation, while Prince Yusupov, one of the Mikhailoviches, was at table with his father, the sound of a horse was heard from the next room. Suddenly, the door was flung o Pietari, Venäjä, Venäjäpen and ther
2 CONC e appeared a horseman with a fine presence, Prince G. Wittgenstein, one of the officers of the Tsar´s escort, an attractive man on whom all the court ladies doted. He held a bouquet of roses which he cast at the feet of the Prince
2 CONC ss. Then he jumped out of the open window and disappeared."
2 CONT
2 CONT                                                                                  Marc Ferro: Nicholas II, The Last of the Tsars
