1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Запись о бракосочетании кн.Константина Александровича Багратион-Мухранского и княжны императорской крови Татьяны Константиновны в присутствии императора Николая II , родителей невесты и её братьев : князей Гавриила
2 CONC , Константина, Игоря и Олега Константиновичей.(ЦГИА Спб, 19-127-1352). г.Павловск. Мариинская придворная церковь.
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%91%D0%B0%D0%B3%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%82%D0%B8%D0%BE%D0%BD-%D0%9C%D1%83%D1%85%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%BD%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9,_%D0%9A%D0%BE%D0%BD%D1%81%D1%82%D0%B0%D0%BD%D1%82%D0%B8%D0%BD_%D0%90%D0%BB%D0%B5%
2 CONC D0%BA%D1%81%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B4%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B8%D1%87 Википедия]
2 CONT
2 CONT Bagration~Mukhranski, Prince Konstantin Aleksandrovich (2.III.1889+19.V.1915).  Educated in the Corps of Pages,  promoted to the Chevalier Gardes Regiment (1909),  appointed Fligel-Adjutant (1913),  as a result of the shortage of 
2 CONC infantry officers he was attached to the 13th "Erivanski" Life~Grenadier Regiment (18.V.1915) as Commander of the 5th Company,  he led that Company into action before Lember a few hours after his arrival in the Regiment and was ki
2 CONC lled.  He was awarded the Order of St. George  4th Class posthumously.  He was married the Princess Tatiana Konstantinovna,  eldest daughter of the Grand Duke Konstantin Konstantinovich on 24.VIII.1911.
